@id n5_ranulf
# DRAFT
# Ranulf at dusk, filling the censers in the choir (night 5, clear and cold). Smooth. (He wears the horned costume.)
# The abbot sick from the smoke; where Ranulf was when Thomas was "attacked" (Suspicion +5); and, if the porter has
# heard from Kit tonight that he bought no candles (lane_kit_5), the wrong question (Suspicion +10): we have all we need.
== start
(Ranulf is filling the censers from his leather bag. The church already smells of it, though Matins is hours off.)
Ranulf {grave}: Porter. Early again. You've made a habit of it.
-> topics

== again
(He hangs a censer on its hook and reaches for the next.)
Ranulf {grave}: Porter.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n5_ranulf_abbot] The abbot can hardly breathe for the smoke. -> abbot
* [if not n5_ranulf_where] Where were you when Brother Thomas was attacked? -> where
* [if lane_kit_5] [if not n5_ranulf_candles] Kit says you bought no candles today, brother. -> candles

== abbot [set n5_ranulf_abbot]
Ranulf {grave, glance}: Then he should breathe deeper. It works on what's in the chest as well as what's in the house.
Ranulf {grave}: Father Abbot ordered it. I only burn it.
-> topics

# The wrong question to the wrong brother (design doc): Suspicion +5.
== where [set n5_ranulf_where] [suspicion 5]
Ranulf {grave, glance}: Here, at my candles, as I am every evening at that hour. I heard the cry, like everyone.
(He doesn't blink.)
Ranulf {cold}: And you, porter? Thomas says you were first through the door. You generally are.
-> topics

# The wrong question to the wrong brother (design doc): Suspicion +10.
== candles [set n5_ranulf_candles] [suspicion 10]
(He stops with a censer in his hand.)
Ranulf {cold}: Kit should mind her tray.
Ranulf {cold}: We have all we need now, porter. That's all.
-> topics

== leave
Ranulf {grave}: In the choir tonight, porter. Breathe deep.
